        "t": "chr",
        "v": [
          "#### Repositories that could not be checked",
          "These repositories are linked in the paper, but their contents could not be retrieved, so nothing below describes them. When the reason is that the platform did not answer, running the check again later may work.",
          "- https://osf.io/parc2: closed registration source",
          "#### Whose Deposits",
          "\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(Repository = c(\"<a href='https://osf.io/regc1' target='_blank'>osf.io/regc1<\/a>\", \n\"<a href='https://osf.io/parc1' target='_blank'>osf.io/parc1<\/a>\", \n\"<a href='https://osf.io/regc2' target='_blank'>osf.io/regc2<\/a>\"\n), \"Cited in\" = c(\"text\", \"text\", \"text\"), Whose = c(\"the authors', for this paper\", \n\"the authors', for this paper\", \"the authors', for this paper\"\n), Why = c(\"a link in the main text, not shown to be anyone else's\", \n\"a link in the main text, not shown to be anyone else's\", \"a link in the main text, not shown to be anyone else's\"\n)), row.names = c(NA, -3L), class = \"data.frame\")\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 10, FALSE)\n```\n",
          "#### Repositories",
          "\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(Repository = c(\"<a href='https://osf.io/parc1' target='_blank'>osf.io/parc1<\/a>\", \n\"<a href='https://osf.io/parc2' target='_blank'>osf.io/parc2<\/a>\"\n), Platform = c(\"osf\", \"osf\"), Error = c(\"private\", \"closed registration source\"\n), \"All Files\" = c(4L, 0L), \"Data Files\" = 1:0, \"Code Files\" = c(2L, \n0L), READMEs = c(0L, 0L), Archives = 1:0), row.names = c(NA, \n-2L), class = c(\"tbl_df\", \"tbl\", \"data.frame\"))\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 10, FALSE)\n```\n",
          "#### Files",
          "\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(Repository = c(\"https://osf.io/parc1\", \"https://osf.io/parc1\", \n\"https://osf.io/parc1\", \"https://osf.io/parc1\"), File = c(\"<a href='https://osf.io/download/6306c5dabe75ef9b1a42a497/' target='_blank'>bad.R<\/a>\", \n\"<a href='https://osf.io/download/uq347/' target='_blank'>bad.Rmd<\/a>\", \n\"<a href='https://osf.io/download/728f26dcbf00a4dc6ff74eaf/' target='_blank'>example2.csv<\/a>\", \n\"<a href='https://osf.io/download/390168dd09634c23320ee85c/' target='_blank'>Archive.zip<\/a>\"\n), Size = c(\"172 B\", \"413 B\", \"5 B\", \"6.4 kB\"), Type = c(\"code\", \n\"code\", \"data\", \"archive\")), row.names = c(NA, -4L), class = \"data.frame\")\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 10, FALSE)\n```\n",
          "#### README Files\n\nREADME files are a way to document the contents and structure of a folder, helping users locate the information they need. You can use a README to document changes to a repository, and explain how files are named. Please consider adding a README to each repository or including 'README' in the name of your overview document.",
          "#### Registration Points to a Closed Project\n\n1 OSF project (https://osf.io/parc2) is referenced by a registration in this manuscript, but it is closed or inaccessible, and no copy of its files could be found anywhere else. Some OSF registrations only describe what was shared, while the actual files live in the project they were registered from — if that project is closed and the registration holds no copy, metacheck cannot list or download its files, and other researchers cannot access them either. Consider making the source project openly available, or re-uploading its files directly into the registration.",
          "#### Unclassified Files\n\nWe could not classify 1 file by name or extension: Archive.zip. Add a recognisable keyword (`data`, `code`, `materials`, `documentation`, `output`) to the file name, or use a common extension, so both humans and machines can tell what kind of file it is.",
          "#### File Naming",
          "File names should be machine-parseable: no spaces or special characters, and every file should be classifiable by name or extension. We found 1 naming problem that should be fixed, and 0 files with a naming suggestion (not required, but a good habit).",
          "\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(File = \"Archive.zip\", Rule = \"unclassifiable\", \n    Severity = \"Required\", Detail = \"could not be classified by name or extension (data_type is 'unknown'); add a recognisable keyword (data, code, materials, ...) or a known extension\"), row.names = c(NA, \n-1L), class = \"data.frame\")\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 10, FALSE)\n```\n",
          "#### File Classification",
          "::: {.callout-note title=\"See how every file was classified and grouped\" collapse=\"true\"}\n\n**code** (2 files)\n\n\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(File = c(\"bad.R\", \"bad.Rmd\"), Group = c(\"ex1\", \n\"ex1\"), Path = c(\"bad.R\", \"bad.Rmd\")), row.names = c(NA, -2L), class = \"data.frame\")\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 10, FALSE)\n```\n\n\n**data** (1 file)\n\n\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(File = \"example2.csv\", Group = \"ex1\", Path = \"example2.csv\"), row.names = c(NA, \n-1L), class = \"data.frame\")\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 10, FALSE)\n```\n\n\n**unknown** (1 file)\n\n\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(File = \"Archive.zip\", Group = \"—\", Path = \"Archive.zip\"), row.names = c(NA, \n-1L), class = \"data.frame\")\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 10, FALSE)\n```\n\n\n:::\n"
